<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!--
      Package version is <pod version>.<binding revision>, e.g. 4.6.2.1 — the same scheme the
      sibling Net.Agora.Android repository uses for its own (Maven Central) line.

      Video binds AgoraRtcEngine_iOS and Voice binds AgoraAudio_iOS — the same engine built
      without the video pipeline, which is the whole point: a voice-only app should not carry
      video codecs it never runs. Agora releases both pods from the same source drop, so the two
      pins are expected to move together; they are separate properties anyway because nothing
      guarantees it.

      Agora ships Android and iOS on independent schedules and the iOS CocoaPods pod for a release
      can lag Maven Central by a point version (verified 2026-07-23: Android's
      io.agora.rtc:full-rtc-basic is at 4.6.3, the newest AgoraRtcEngine_iOS pod published is
      4.6.2) — the fetch scripts check this against CocoaPods trunk before downloading. So the iOS
      and Android package versions for the same product are not expected to match, any more than
      DatadogNet.iOS and DatadogNet.Android's do.

      The fourth component belongs to this repository and advances when the binding changes while
      the native artifact stays put.
    -->
    <AgoraVideoIosVersion>4.6.2</AgoraVideoIosVersion>
    <AgoraVideoBindingRevision>5</AgoraVideoBindingRevision>
    <AgoraVoiceIosVersion>4.6.2</AgoraVoiceIosVersion>
    <AgoraVoiceBindingRevision>5</AgoraVoiceBindingRevision>
    <!--
      Signaling (RTM) is a different product with its own native version line — 2.2.x, nothing to
      do with the RTC 4.6.x line above. See build/BuildNugets.sh for how releases handle packages
      whose versions do not move together.
    -->
    <AgoraSignalingIosVersion>2.2.6</AgoraSignalingIosVersion>
    <AgoraSignalingBindingRevision>3</AgoraSignalingBindingRevision>
    <!--
      The RTM zip bundles its own aosl.framework, at a version that trails the one the RTC pods
      bundle — 1.2.13 against 1.3.5, and the older one does not export aosl_ref_magic, which
      AgoraRtcKit resolves at load. Every package that ships an aosl.framework puts it at the same
      path in the consuming app's bundle, so exactly one copy survives and every product in that
      app has to run against it. When the survivor was Signaling's, the RTC engine could not load
      at all. The bundled copy is therefore discarded and aosl comes from AgoraInfra_iOS — the
      pod Chat already takes it from — at 1.3.5, which is the aosl the RTC pods bundle byte for
      byte, so a Video + Signaling app now genuinely carries one library rather than two that
      merely get along.

      Pinned separately from AgoraChatInfraIosVersion below, which deliberately reads 1.3.9: the
      two products' infra requirements are unrelated and a Chat bump must not silently move this
      one. That the mixture is safe is not assumed either — AoslCompatibilityTests checks every
      shipped aosl against every aosl symbol the three SDK frameworks actually import.
    -->
    <AgoraSignalingInfraIosVersion>1.3.5</AgoraSignalingInfraIosVersion>
    <!--
      Chat is a third product on a third native line — 1.4.x. Its pod is Agora_Chat_iOS, not the
      AgoraChat pod on CocoaPods trunk: that one is the abandoned 3.8.x Easemob line and has
      nothing to do with this release. Unlike the RTC pods, Agora_Chat_iOS does not bundle aosl —
      it declares AgoraInfra_iOS as a dependency, so the fetch script downloads two archives and
      that pod's version is pinned separately here.
    -->
    <!--
      Whiteboard is netless's, not Agora's own: Agora acquired the product and still documents it,
      but the source and the releases are netless-io's. Its iOS line runs ahead of the Android one
      (2.16.137 vs 2.16.123) — they are separate repositories with separate release cadences, so
      unlike the RTC products there is no reason to expect them to meet.
    -->
    <AgoraWhiteboardIosVersion>2.16.137</AgoraWhiteboardIosVersion>
    <AgoraWhiteboardBindingRevision>2</AgoraWhiteboardBindingRevision>
    <!--
      Fastboard is netless's UI layer over the Interactive Whiteboard, on its own line. Unlike every
      other product here it is Swift, so what this repository binds is not the SDK but the
      Objective-C shim in native/AgoraFastboardBridge — see build/build-fastboard.sh. It carries its
      own copy of the whiteboard library, and that copy's version comes from
      native/AgoraFastboardBridge/Package.resolved, not from AgoraWhiteboardIosVersion above.
    -->
    <AgoraFastboardIosVersion>1.4.6</AgoraFastboardIosVersion>
    <AgoraFastboardBindingRevision>1</AgoraFastboardBindingRevision>
    <AgoraChatIosVersion>1.4.0</AgoraChatIosVersion>
    <AgoraChatInfraIosVersion>1.3.9</AgoraChatInfraIosVersion>
    <AgoraChatBindingRevision>3</AgoraChatBindingRevision>
    <!--
      The default for projects that do not pick their own line (tests, and the Video binding
      itself); the Voice .csproj overrides this with its own pair.
    -->
    <VersionPrefix>$(AgoraVideoIosVersion).$(AgoraVideoBindingRevision)</VersionPrefix>

    <Authors>s.bokatuk</Authors>
    <Company>s.bokatuk</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright © s.bokatuk</Copyright>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/sbokatuk/Net.Agora.iOS</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/sbokatuk/Net.Agora.iOS</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <!--
      MIT covers the binding code in this repository. Agora's own SDK is distributed under Agora's
      SDK licence terms (not an OSI-approved licence with its own SPDX identifier), so — unlike
      DatadogNet.iOS's "MIT AND Apache-2.0" — no second licence expression is added here; nothing
      is claimed about Agora's own terms.
    -->
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>

    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition=" '$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' == 'true' ">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
